  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know mean free path</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>N = no. of molecule</p><p>V = volume of container</p><p>d = diameter of molecule</p><p>Velocity constant and no. of molecules are same. So mean free path remains same. As temperature increases no. of collision increases so relaxation time decrease.</p>",
